+
+## Rate limiting
+
+`createServer({ rateLimit: { limit, windowMs } })`. Defaults: `{ limit: 60, windowMs: 60000 }`, each field defaults on its own. Both must be positive safe integers; invalid values make `createServer` throw.
+
+- Timing uses the server's `now` option.
+- Limiting runs before routing and authentication, so 401 and 404 responses are counted too.
+- Key: the `x-api-key` header. Requests without it, or with an empty value, share the key `anonymous`.
+- Windows are fixed and per key. A window starts at the key's first request and lasts `windowMs`. The first `limit` requests in a window are allowed. Once `windowMs` has elapsed, the next request starts a new window.
+- Rejected requests get `429` with `Retry-After` (whole seconds until the window ends, rounded up, minimum 1) and body `{"error": "rate_limited", "retryAfter": N}`, where N is the same value as `Retry-After`.
+- Every limited response carries `X-RateLimit-Limit` and `X-RateLimit-Remaining` (requests left in the window after this one, never below 0).
+- `GET /health` is exempt: never limited, never counted, no rate-limit headers.
